+// ---- the multipart commit protocol's seeded crash/race properties (issue #508) ----
+//
+// Proposal 0016's publication, restore-fence and repoint paths are new **destructive and
+// concurrent** paths, so AGENTS.md's *Test fidelity* rule makes seeded Tier-0 coverage a merge
+// requirement. Each property below drives the REAL batch builders (`wyrd_core::multipart`) and
+// the REAL maintenance passes over the trait seams — never a re-implementation — and closes with
+// the **classification sweep**: after the scenario, a restore pass must mark NOTHING stranded,
+// which is the public observable of invariant (2)'s *no-gaps* claim (`0016:2911-2924`). Note the
+// sweep is deliberately not a partition assertion: this protocol overlaps protection across
+// every handoff (a published chunk is committed-referenced *and* still `part:`-named until the
+// records obligation drains), and a disjointness assertion would fail correct executions (X94).
