+    /// it was never created, was cancelled, or its tombstone answered a *different*
+    /// assembly.
+    UnknownUpload,
+    /// The session is fenced by a publication already in progress. At most one publisher
+    /// at a time is a guarantee, not an accident: a second concurrent completer is a
+    /// conflict, never a parallel resume.
+    UploadBusy,
+    /// An admission ceiling refused the request — too many parts in flight for this
+    /// upload, or too many uploads open across the deployment. Backpressure, not an error.
+    Overloaded,
+    /// A named part is absent, or its recorded digest does not match the one named.
+    PartMissingOrMismatched,
+    /// The named parts were not in ascending part-number order.
+    PartsOutOfOrder,
+    /// A non-final part is below the minimum a part may be.
+    PartTooSmall,
+    /// A part, or the assembled object, exceeds what this deployment is configured to
+    /// publish. Surfaced rather than hit at the backend: a refusal, never an
+    /// over-envelope commit.
+    TooLarge,
+    /// A malformed argument (a part number outside the legal range, an unparsable id).
+    InvalidArgument(String),
+    /// The target container has no record.
+    NoSuchContainer,
+    /// The publication compare-and-set lost to concurrent writes on the target key more
+    /// times than the bound allows. The session is left usable and the client may retry
+    /// without re-uploading a part.
